Optimizing Argo CD Performance
Objectives
Design and deploy a production-grade Argo CD installation on a local Kubernetes cluster with Redis caching tuned for throughput
Implement and validate sync policy optimizations including server-side apply, resource exclusions, and sync waves across multiple applications
Measure and compare synchronization performance between baseline and optimized Argo CD configurations using scripted benchmarks
Prerequisites
Comfort with Ubuntu command-line operations including file editing, process management, and reading command output
Conceptual understanding of Kubernetes objects (Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps) and GitOps principles
Lab Environment
You will work on a dedicated AWS EC2 Ubuntu instance provided by Al Nafi. The instance has a base Ubuntu installation; you will install all required tools in Task 1.

